# LOGIC SEPARATION (HOOK-FIRST)

## 1. The "Screen-is-a-Controller" Rule

- Screens (`src/screens/...`) must ONLY contain layout and event handlers.
- All complex logic, state calculations, and API interactions MUST live in a custom hook.

## 2. Hook Naming & Location

- Feature-specific hooks: `src/screens/[feature]/hooks/use[Feature]Logic.ts`.
- Reusable hooks: `src/hooks/`.
- Hooks must return a structured object: `{ data, states, handlers }`.

## 3. Side Effects

- `useEffect` usage in screens is discouraged. Move the effect into the custom hook.
- Give every `useEffect` a comment explaining _why_ it is necessary.
